{"findings":[{"rule_id":"WPS-004","evidence":[{"kind":"dimension","ref":"D12","page":1,"quote":"⌀ 16 H7 (+0.018/0)"},{"kind":"title_block","ref":"surface_treatment","page":1,"quote":"I.Z.B.P. (TRIVALENT)"}],"comment":"The ⌀16 H7 hole (D12) is a tight-tolerance fit feature, but the drawing does not state whether the H7 limits apply before or after the I.Z.B.P. plating; plating buildup will reduce the bore and can cause assembly interference. The designer should add a note specifying that the H7 tolerance applies after plating, or pre-plate the hole oversize to compensate for coating thickness."
  ,
"recommended_correction":"Add a note such as 'H7 TOLERANCE APPLIES AFTER PLATING' or specify an adjusted pre-plate diameter accounting for the I.Z.B.P. coating thickness."}]}
